{"type":"target-event","projectId":"000458-native-ch31-seq104","event":{"type":"proposal","proposal":{"summary":"Revise ch31-seq104 into a 3-part English script that follows the recovered Good Samaritan excerpt: a developed reflection on the rarity of true charity, a causal bridge to the viewer’s response, and a brief settle. Keep canonical roles separate and preserve the excerpt’s qualifiers and concrete anchors without inventing source footage or subtitles.","command":{"projectId":"000458-native-ch31-seq104","expectedRevision":1,"idempotencyKey":"f1b4e5e7-a8d9-426d-b50f-7f3611947c14","operations":[{"kind":"set-text","itemId":"reflection","text":"The parable begins with a lawyer’s question, “Who is my neighbour?” and that question matters, because it sets the drift of the whole story. Jesus does not answer with an allegory hunt or a clever detour. He shows a wounded traveler, then a priest and a Levite who see him and pass by on the other side. That is a plain picture of how rare true brotherly love is. Much charity is easy to admire when it costs little. But the love this parable commends is different: it notices real distress, refuses excuses, and will not measure a person’s worthiness before helping."},{"kind":"set-speech","itemId":"reflection","speech":{"text":"The parable begins with a lawyer’s question, “Who is my neighbour?” and that question matters, because it sets the drift of the whole story. Jesus does not answer with an allegory hunt or a clever detour. He shows a wounded traveler, then a priest and a Levite who see him and pass by on the other side. That is a plain picture of how rare true brotherly love is. Much charity is easy to admire when it costs little. But the love this parable commends is different: it notices real distress, refuses excuses, and will not measure a person’s worthiness before helping.","role":"reflection","suppressed":false,"voice":{"assetId":"fbad58bb-cefa-4c27-a01e-0ef0fa93ba92","versionId":"cmtretxe100042ctenx3jrmih","digest":"f88fcf65aa78e5c9cd5e9babe48ed2f6838b80fface62d77b3930cf8d11a5b2a"},"provider":"elevenlabs","model":"eleven_multilingual_v2","settings":{"speed":1,"style":0,"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.75,"use_speaker_boost":true},"pronunciation":null}},{"kind":"set-text","itemId":"bridge","text":"And that is why the Samaritan changes the point of the story. He does not ask whether the man belongs to his circle, and he does not wait for a safer moment. He draws near, gives aid, and turns compassion into action. If that is the lesson, then the question cannot stay abstract. It presses on conscience: what is real charity, who counts as a neighbour, and whether we will do good when it costs time, trouble, and care."},{"kind":"set-speech","itemId":"bridge","speech":{"text":"And that is why the Samaritan changes the point of the story. He does not ask whether the man belongs to his circle, and he does not wait for a safer moment. He draws near, gives aid, and turns compassion into action. If that is the lesson, then the question cannot stay abstract. It presses on conscience: what is real charity, who counts as a neighbour, and whether we will do good when it costs time, trouble, and care.","role":"bridge","suppressed":false,"voice":{"assetId":"fbad58bb-cefa-4c27-a01e-0ef0fa93ba92","versionId":"cmtretxe100042ctenx3jrmih","digest":"f88fcf65aa78e5c9cd5e9babe48ed2f6838b80fface62d77b3930cf8d11a5b2a"},"provider":"elevenlabs","model":"eleven_multilingual_v2","settings":{"speed":1,"style":0,"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.75,"use_speaker_boost":true},"pronunciation":null}},{"kind":"set-text","itemId":"settle","text":"Take a quiet breath. Let that question stay."},{"kind":"set-speech","itemId":"settle","speech":{"text":"Take a quiet breath. Let that question stay.","role":"settle","suppressed":false,"voice":{"assetId":"fbad58bb-cefa-4c27-a01e-0ef0fa93ba92","versionId":"cmtretxe100042ctenx3jrmih","digest":"f88fcf65aa78e5c9cd5e9babe48ed2f6838b80fface62d77b3930cf8d11a5b2a"},"provider":"elevenlabs","model":"eleven_multilingual_v2","settings":{"speed":1,"style":0,"stability":0.5,"similarity_boost":0.75,"use_speaker_boost":true},"pronunciation":null}},{"kind":"set-metadata","title":"ch31-seq104 — good Samaritan reflection","language":"en","durationInFrames":2700}]},"quality":{"coverage":[{"role":"reflection","status":"present","itemIds":["reflection"]},{"role":"bridge","status":"present","itemIds":["bridge"]},{"role":"settle","status":"present","itemIds":["settle"]},{"role":"recap","status":"absent","itemIds":[]},{"role":"question","status":"absent","itemIds":[]},{"role":"prayer","status":"absent","itemIds":[]}],"findings":[{"criterion":"coherence","status":"pass","reason":"The script moves from the lawyer’s question to the rarity of true brotherly love, then causally to the Samaritan’s corrective example, and ends with a short settle that leaves the listener with the conscience question rather than a repeat summary.","itemIds":["reflection","bridge","settle"],"sources":[{"assetId":"c480bf29-5659-4ff1-b08c-fccfc5c16c5a","versionId":"cmtrhx33100032c767cd2d68v","digest":"2e2ef497ab4140435ccb3659f98f042f6a01c1b237b4216aa58b3864943c0ab5"}]},{"criterion":"depth","status":"pass","reason":"The adaptation retains the excerpt’s developed reasoning: the parable is not treated as an allegory hunt, charity is contrasted with easier low-cost benevolence, and the Samaritan’s action is presented as a practical correction that presses on conscience.","itemIds":["reflection","bridge"],"sources":[{"assetId":"c480bf29-5659-4ff1-b08c-fccfc5c16c5a","versionId":"cmtrhx33100032c767cd2d68v","digest":"2e2ef497ab4140435ccb3659f98f042f6a01c1b237b4216aa58b3864943c0ab5"}]},{"criterion":"fidelity","status":"pass","reason":"No invented footage, citations, or source-subtitle claims were added. The script preserves the recovered excerpt’s core anchors: the lawyer’s question, the wounded traveler, the priest and Levite passing by, and the Samaritan’s active compassion.","itemIds"